# 7. What is a DataFrame?

A DataFrame is a 2-dimensional table in Pandas.

It looks similar to an Excel sheet.

Example

| Name    | Age | Marks |
| ------- | --- | ----- |
| Utkarsh | 20  | 95    |
| Rahul   | 21  | 88    |

Whenever we read a CSV file using read_csv(), Pandas stores the data inside a DataFrame.

